# What this patch contains:
#   This ONE patch carries TWO independent detectors, so a single build serves both
#   issue specs. They are told apart by their `match` regex, never by the toolchain.
#
#   REVERT: restores the pre-fix GVN behaviour for both bugs (shared-reference deref
#           unification, and reuse of a cached deref load across a deref store).
#   DETECT: `rustc-130853` fires when GVN unifies two dereferences of a shared reference;
#           `rustc-132353` fires on the deref-reuse, place-reuse and aggregate-to-copy
#           rewrites (three sub-sites, all under the same match prefix).
#
# Reproduce:
#   git clone https://github.com/rust-lang/rust.git patch-132353
#   cd patch-132353 && git checkout 6b00bc388019
#   git apply /path/to/patch-132353.rust.patch
#   ./x build --stage 1 compiler
#   rustup toolchain link patch-132353 build/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/stage1
#
# Verify the detector is live:
#   MISCOMP_LOG=/tmp/m.log ZEROOS_GUEST_TOOLCHAIN=patch-132353 <build a guest>
#   grep -c '^MISCOMP rustc-130853' /tmp/m.log
